<article class="env-lemma" id="01H7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01H7">Lemma <span data-tag="01H7">25.11.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\mathcal{B}$ be a basis for the topology of $X$. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ is quasi-compact, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
each $U \in \mathcal{B}$ is quasi-compact open, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the intersection of any two quasi-compact opens in $X$ is quasi-compact. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists a hypercovering $(I, \{ U_ i\} )$ of $X$ with the following properties </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
each $U_ i$ is an element of the basis $\mathcal{B}$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
each of the $I_ n$ is a finite set, and in particular 
</p>
</li><li><p>
each of the coverings (<a href="/tag/01H2" data-tag="01H2">25.11.0.1</a>), (<a href="/tag/01H3" data-tag="01H3">25.11.0.2</a>), and (<a href="/tag/01H4" data-tag="01H4">25.11.0.3</a>) is finite. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows directly from the construction in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/01H6" data-tag="01H6">25.11.3</a> if we choose finite coverings by elements of $\mathcal{B}$ in (<a href="/tag/071K" data-tag="071K">25.11.3.1</a>). Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>